## SECTION 1: THE THESIS SHIFT

The IP valuation document proved one thing: CrisPRO decoded why six trials failed.

That is worth $40.5M in current portfolio rNPV and $101–340M in platform value.

It is not worth $500M.

**What gets to $500M is proving CrisPRO can make the corrected trials work.**

The difference between a decoder and an enabler is not scientific — it is operational. A decoder tells you what went wrong. An enabler provides the patient selection algorithm, the companion diagnostic protocol, the biomarker scoring threshold, the IST design, and the data analysis that turns a CRISPR-validated hypothesis into a clinical signal. That is what pharma pays $125M upfront for. That is what justifies a $500M Series A/B valuation.

**The Repare benchmark:** Repare Therapeutics raised at ~$400M Series B on ONE CRISPR-validated SL asset (camonsertib) and a platform thesis. Roche paid $125M upfront for that single asset in 2022. Repare had no clinical data at Series B — only CRISPR functional genomics and a Phase I IND.

**CrisPRO's position vs. Repare at Series B:**

| Dimension | Repare at Series B | CrisPRO at Series B target |
|---|---|---|
| CRISPR-validated SL assets | 1 (camonsertib) | 2 (BRIEF-1, BRIEF-4) |
| Additional assets | 0 | 2 (BRIEF-2, BRIEF-3) |
| Clinical data | Phase I IND filed | IST interim data (ZEB1-high NSCLC BrM, n=10–15) |
| Revenue | Pre-revenue | $42M in signed upfront deals |
| Business model | Drug developer (holds IND) | Asset-light IP licensor (never holds IND) |
| Graveyard pipeline | De novo discovery | 500+ decoded trials, 8 briefs/year throughput |
| Live pharma partner | None at Series B | Brenus Pharma (BreAK CRC-001 active) |

**The $500M valuation is not a stretch. It is a 25% premium over Repare's Series B on a materially stronger evidence base and a structurally superior business model.**

