### Stream 1: IP Licensing (Pharma-Sponsored Trials)

**What CrisPRO sells:** Method-of-treatment patent claim + companion diagnostic claim + mechanism rationale package (failure autopsy + DepMap analysis + biomarker scoring protocol + deal structure term sheet).

**What the pharma partner gets:** The patient selection logic for a drug they already own. They run the trial under their IND. CrisPRO collects upfront + milestones + royalties.

**Why pharma pays:** Licensing CrisPRO's IP is 10–50x cheaper than running a new Phase III from scratch. The original sponsor has already spent $150–500M on the drug. The safety data exists. The manufacturing process exists. The only missing piece is the patient selection logic — which CrisPRO has.

**The competitive tension play:** Approach original sponsor first with 60-day right of first negotiation. If no engagement, approach competitor. Both parties know this. The patent clock is running. The urgency is structural, not manufactured.

